WEBVTT

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.520
Thanks.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.480
That's a nice photo.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:41.660
TURN OVER

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.420
Feels like a whole different place.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.550
Sort of... oppressive.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.390
I don't wanna eat that.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.530
The smell of oil and steel...

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.290
A smog of despair and dismay.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.700
And jeez, the checkpoint guards were a pain in the ass. I thought they'd never let us through.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.320
It's a shame your shoes won't be ready in time,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.000
but an exhibition match is perfect for your debut.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.700
There's no better place to get a feel for what a real match is like.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.910
Still... Why must I pretend I'm a Bigfoot?

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:30.070
Well, honestly... if it comes out that you're a giant, explaining it will be a huge hassle.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.920
Just bear with it a little while.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.090
I'm not familiar with that Bigfoot.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.430
A new type?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.300
You look well, Haruka.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.410
It's our new rookie.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.660
I'm having him debut in today's game.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.400
This entire town is the court for this match.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.360
Your movements are completely unrestricted.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.770
What about spectators?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.210
It's complicated.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.160
At the moment the Lunatic Company has this town under martial law.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.320
Carrying on, basket A is there.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.200
The Earthdash branch of Lunatic.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.450
Basket B is at a place you know very well, young lady.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.600
The house where you once lived with your mother, Sela D. Miranda.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.870
That's the second goal.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.860
I don't get it. What do you think you're doing?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.140
Hold on...

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.650
I didn't make the decision, they did.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.090
Your opponents, the Old-Timers.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.240
They're local amateur Basquashers.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.200
You...

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.510
They decided placement of the goals.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.360
It's an exhibition match against amateurs, after all...

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.210
There's nothing wrong with letting them give you a little handicap.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.840
Rosso, Giaro, Bianco...

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.920
It's been a long time, Miss Sela.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.090
Rosso, doing this for a joke is rude.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.300
Sela?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.870
They worked for that man.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.480
They taught me basketball.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.770
Miss, you shouldn't call your father "that man."

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.090
At any rate, it seems introductions will be unnecessary.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.320
Without further ado, the exhibition special!

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.820
Basket A, Team Basquash!

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.280
Basket B, the Old-Timers!

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.600
Their quarter-length match will now begin!

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.200
Damn!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:38.930
Bianco!

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.300
What are you really plotting?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.780
I'm just doing my utmost to ensure that you can all happily go to Mooneyes.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.370
James Lone...

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:05.120
Do you really think this farce will move the kingdom and the moon to act again?

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.260
Too easy, old man!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:25.640
What?!

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:27.720
Rosso!

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.720
Nice miss!

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:35.860
Sela!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:42.560
Bastard!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.080
Dan!

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.710
Nice one, Navi!

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:55.580
Rosso?

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.140
Miss Sela,

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.840
isn't it about time you figured out what the Don was feeling?

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.250
What?  So it matters now?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.600
He abandoned me and Mom!

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.300
I bet he's happy he got killed for the sake of the Family!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:15.900
I don't let anyone get away with that kind of degenerate disrespect, not even the Don's daughter.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.030
For old fogeys, they're really not bad.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:26.470
What decides winners and losers in Basquash isn't physical ability, it's technique and feel.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.700
Momentum alone won't take you to the top.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.580
Dan!

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.500
Shit!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.010
What the hell are these guys?

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.600
Ouch.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.260
They aren't doing anything special.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.440
They're just sticking to the fundamentals.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.720
But their level is incredibly high...

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:01.230
Deciding in an instant and reacting with precision.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.690
You little...

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.330
So they're a tough nut to crack.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.900
It's a wide world.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.040
You gotta be kidding me!

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.870
So then we just gotta think faster and move faster than these old men!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:20.910
Sela!

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.550
Dan?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.010
Nice pass!

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.040
Dan, help Sela!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:33.560
Quick!

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.390
Got it!

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:35.060
Roger!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.140
Sela!

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:41.890
Navi?

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.380
This time, Dan's the screener!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.070
I can't believe it!

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.950
Change a person's environment, and sometimes you trigger a metamorphosis.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.040
Isn't it time you figured out what the Don was feeling?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.050
There, Miss!

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.260
Slam dunk!

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:16.680
Navi!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:18.560
Sela!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.600
Take it up!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.230
Basquat the hell out of it!

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.430
Sela!

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.610
Sela...

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.640
Basquash!

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:52.820
Incredible...

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.070
Speaking.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.630
You did it after all, James.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:01.260
If it isn't General Manager Yan.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.980
I'm glad to know you're unharmed.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.460
Thank you for your concern.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.860
Still, I never suspected this from you.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.200
Pardon? I'm not sure what you mean.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.610
Don't try to fool me.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:18.820
Every facility destroyed in that game was part of the Turbine City redevelopment project!

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.100
This is without a doubt a terrorist act.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.560
No, you're wrong.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.160
This is a sport.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.610
Pretentious basketball lowlifes!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.970
Don't think you'll get away with it!

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:40.910
Game over. Game over.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.430
Game over.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.570
That was a picture-perfect dunk, Miss Sela.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.010
Rosso.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:00.040
I won't ask you to think of the Don's feelings any more.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.800
Someday when the time is right, I think you'll understand.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.880
I'm not surprised, Dunk Mask.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.170
It's your team's victory.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.300
We'll have to do this again sometime.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.650
Well, yeah!

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.660
The basquashing heart is always young!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.350
Yeah, even if you got one foot in the grave.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.160
That call you took after Sela dunked...

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.390
You mean, they might croak on the court?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.400
A town exploited for conflict...

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:33.240
I don't think that girl's father wanted any part of such a town.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.580
Do you?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.360
To steal lives... to even steal voices raised in joy...

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:48.080
What do you hate that much, Yan Harris?

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:57.450
Navi.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.990
Um, I, uh...

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.130
You played well today.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.430
I'll raise my opinion of you, a little.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.100
I'm glad.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.860
But if you peek at me in the bath, I will not forgive you.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.570
That was an accident.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:14.740
Idiot!

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.990
About that photograph...

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.450
Photograph?

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.950
Why did you say it was a nice photo?

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.240
You were laughing as if you were having fun.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.330
You looked happy.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.910
Oh.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.500
Yeah.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.970
Thanks, Navi.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:40.730
Sela?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.600
That's good, Sela.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.230
Sela, be happy.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.570
Daddy!

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.890
The first time I ever saw a ball...

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.890
He spun the basketball on his fingertip for us.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.660
Wow!

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:25.140
Coco, you might have the makings of a professional basketball player.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.890
Yeah! That's what I'm gonna be!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.750
If you're a truly fine player... That's right.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.870
Huh? What?

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.490
I'll take you with me to the moon.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:42.280
Every day was fun. I was happy.

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:46.410
I just dribbled as hard as I could, aiming for the basket.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.110
It hurts!

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:54.800
Coco!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.770
With the present he gave me...

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.810
My world expanded.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:14.470
I learned how to work on the Net and earn a living.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.770
To lighten my brother's burden.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.910
My brother changed after my injury.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:23.910
You're going down,

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.720
BFB!

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.820
"Bigfoot Basketball is coming to Rollingtown:

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:39.140
Rolling Arena's Inaugural Game BFB League Regulars Match"?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.930
I'll crush them.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:47.620
You really do hate Bigfoots, don't you?

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.470
The giant-footed mechs that stole Coco's future, huh?

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.420
I'm home!

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:58.010
Coco, today I got you a present
 you're gonna like for sure!

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.570
What do you think it is?

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.990
I came first.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.400
Try guessing, Coco!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.350
He would do anything for me.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.900
He worked his heart out for me.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:08.360
It felt heavy, like I couldn't breathe.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:14.620
The only thing I could do for him was refuse.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.240
Even if that meant hurting him.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:55.710
Miyuki gave my brother a chance.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:04.340
And that became the catalyst for street-style BFB to explode on Earthdash.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.020
Go!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.750
Sorry, but this is as far as you get!

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.750
Stop it!

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.970
I don't wanna remember!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:48.760
Ow!

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.930
Ow! I'm gonna die!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:54.190
Come on, get a grip...

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.680
Just stop it, please!

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:21.830
Rouge!

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:24.370
Rouge!

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:25.270
Now!

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:27.420
A three-pointer!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.190
There, you finally got some points.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:55.870
Showdown time, Idol Red!

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.660
Don't cry when you lose!

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.330
Bring it on!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.920
Citron, head him off!

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.440
You won't get past!

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:06.600
Mine!

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:07.330
What?!

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.670
Gotcha!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:15.180
Destroy!

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:23.230
But... How did my brother master a Bigfoot so quickly?

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.070
Okay then!

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:31.280
Luck? Talent?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:33.860
I have a feeling it isn't that simple.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.450
Not a patient guy!

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:38.870
Is that your whole strategy?!

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:40.580
Not quite!

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:43.920
Come on! Now we're really gonna get started!

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.010
Is that... the legendary...?

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.250
The legend...

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.530
Long, long ago,

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:04.980
in an age of myth, the Gods dashed through the depths of space.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:10.110
They would grab a star, stealing it back and forth, vying for absolute supremacy.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.570
And one day...

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:14.320
One of them dunked it right into this world.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.210
At the end of their furious struggle,

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:21.620
the gods' footprints became the seas and the rivers,

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:25.950
and the marks left by the dunk became the cornerstones of civilization.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.320
Open City Basketball!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.050
This is the birth of a new sport!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.320
So this is the street style!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.670
It's as entertaining as I thought!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.400
It would be a waste to let butterfingered amateurs have all the fun!

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.200
Dumbass! {ep7}

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.500
Court? Rules? Referee?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.160
Nothing about this basketball is "open" or "city"!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.330
Watch.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:10.310
This is Basquash!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:11.340
Like this!

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:19.220
These cramped, little lines can eat shit!

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:22.350
We don't <i>have</i> bounds!

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:25.980
This...

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.770
...is my answer!

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:33.650
Basquash!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.740
Did you get that, you bubble-blowing bastard?

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:45.520
I confirm that I've received your answer!

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:48.620
Dunk Mask is banned for life!

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.340
Dumbass!

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.960
It's no hardship to be banned from a group I never joined!

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.110
Oh, that's right.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.860
I forgot one.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:18:59.760
Here!

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:18.740
The people from the moon are seeking the legend's power.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.710
They tried to become the legend, but didn't make it.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.290
I flunked out long before they did though.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:30.720
That was truly a tragedy.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.880
The moon might look like a unified monolith, but that's far from the case.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.400
An opposing group set that trap...

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.930
It wasn't an accident.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.550
They were stupid.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.110
It was no time to be squabbling over leadership.

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.260
Thanks to them the plan was delayed for years.

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:58.260
But thanks to that, my brother is basquatting.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.590
Basquatting, is he?

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.000
Taking a zigzagging path down a straight line.

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.200
Becoming a fierce and burning power.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.530
Beautiful.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.920
It's closer again.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.500
As if you could reach out and touch the city lights...

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:21.090
That's Dan, isn't it?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:24.700
Thank you.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:29.890
For taking me with you to the moon.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:32.060
I promised, didn't I?

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:35.560
If you became a fine player, I'd take you.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.990
That is your Basquash, isn't it?

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:45.280
You're a truly fine player.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.090
Basquash...

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:55.190
Area zero,

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:56.860
the place where everything began.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.500
<b></b>

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.500
<b></b>

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.740
Area zero,

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.810
that sad place.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:01.750
But,

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.850
we must go!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:07.930
Next time: Fit In Break

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:08.200
NEXT TIME

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:08.200
FIT IN 

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.200
BREAK
